  "scientific_and_runtime_qualifications_v4": {
    "cpython_itimer_real_vs_forked_os_worker_sigkill_precision": "In CPython, signal.setitimer(signal.ITIMER_REAL, ...) delivers SIGALRM to the C signal handler, which sets a pending flag checked at Python bytecode evaluation boundaries (PyErr_CheckSignals()) or when an interruptible OS syscall returns EINTR. Consequently, DeadlineController.itimer_guard() is a secondary parent-side fallback and cannot preempt an uninterruptible C/Rust/CUDA extension mid-call without returning to the Python eval loop or an interruptible syscall. Hard wall-clock preemption of worker work is enforced by DeadlineController.run_batch_in_killable_workers(), which runs work in forked OS worker process groups (os.setpgrp()) and terminates them immediately at the OS kernel level via os.killpg(pid, signal.SIGKILL) + os.kill(pid, signal.SIGKILL) + proc.join().",
